Chapter 13
The IMA Statement: four principles, four standards
بيان الممارسة المهنية الأخلاقية: أربعة مبادئ وأربعة معايير
Chapter 12 described ethics in general. This chapter is about the specific document that binds you: the IMA Statement of Ethical Professional Practice, which every member and every certificate holder agrees to follow, and which the exam tests by giving you a situation and asking which standards it engages.
The Statement is short. It sets out four overarching principles that describe the values, and four standards that describe conduct, each with its specific obligations. Learning it as eight headings is enough to recognise them; learning what each obligation actually requires is what earns the marks, because the examiners write situations in which two or three standards are engaged at once and the answer must say which and why.
Figure F813-01 is your map.
Figure F813-01. Chapter 13 roadmap: four principles, four standards, and how to apply them to a situation.
